  "Id": 1705,
  "Title": "ELE_net courses in East Africa",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "ELE_net has been offering blended courses to address specific students\u2019 needs.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass4B282940CFFF44E7B3BF8DD70C866D75\"><p></p></div>In addition to the online courses that AKU students in East Africa can take to help them develop their academic writing skills in English, ELE_net has been offering blended courses to address specific students\u2019 needs.<br><br>In 2018, IED students in Dar es Salaam had the opportunity to take the Language Accuracy in Writing and the Integrating Academic Reading into Writing courses through a blended approach - a mix of face-to-face teaching and online study. Also, following a recent ELE_net visit to Uganda and Kenya, the Network is now remotely delivering courses specifically tailored to SONAM students in Nairobi. These include academic reading and writing, and a new English for Presentations course, which will be offered to students during the last year of their bachelor\u2019s degree.<br><br>",
